# A gap in vstd's memory model (raw permissions carry no byte values); the
# harness reads the eight zero bytes as a u64.
axiom_zero_word	raw pointer (internal)	Kani	discharged (Kani: kani_proofs::zero::zero_word_reads_zero)
# A `Zeroed` token is not tied to the writes to its bytes; each caller
# pairs a permission with a token whose bytes nothing wrote since it was
# made: cut together under one lock hold, or as `Meta::alloc_zeroed`
# returns them (`Table::storage`).
ZeroRaw::axiom_new	allocator invariant	none (assumption)
# vstd states no effect of write_bytes: the bytes read as zero after.
zero_raw	raw pointer (internal)	Kani	discharged (Kani: kani_proofs::ptr::zero_raw_fills)
